  "observations": [
    "Both models use three GDN layers followed by one attention layer. Dense 27B has 64 target layers: 48 GDN and 16 full attention. Flash-Next has 48: 36 GDN and 12 QSA attention layers.",
    "Both have 24 attention query heads of width 256, and identical GDN head counts, dimensions and convolution width. Dense 27B has 4 KV heads versus 2 for Flash-Next; hidden width is 5120 versus 2560.",
    "Dense 27B applies one width-17408 gated MLP per layer. Flash-Next routes each token to 10 of 512 width-640 experts, adds a width-640 shared expert, and carries four residual streams. Selected-expert count is not the number of distinct experts reached by a batch.",
    "Flash-Next adds PLE at configured layer 2 (zero-based 1), a QSA indexer, and a sigmoid GDN output gate. Its selection retains every block at KV lengths <=2051. Decode and paged verification still use the sparse kernel machinery at short contexts; mathematical equivalence to dense attention does not identify the executed kernel.",
    "The architecture differences change matrix shapes, routing, state handling and memory access. Configs alone do not attribute the measured scaling gap to a cause or establish a hardware limit.",
    "MTP metadata is included because both checkpoints ship a one-layer head. It does not imply MTP was enabled in the target-only dense controls."
  ],
